33
00:01:28,230 --> 00:01:28,230
(Beau) Earth.

34
00:01:28,231 --> 00:01:34,050
(Beau) It has been countless millennia
since this world was ruled by humans.

35
00:01:35,910 --> 00:01:38,572
(Beau) They once danced
in light, and they once

36
00:01:38,573 --> 00:01:44,370
(Beau) touched the sky, opening
the doors to heaven.

37
00:01:47,890 --> 00:01:51,730
(Beau) But in an instant, it ended.

38
00:01:51,731 --> 00:01:55,730
(Beau) Alien invaders from
deep in the cosmos arrived

39
00:01:55,731 --> 00:02:01,170
(Beau) through the gates and rained
an inferno upon their garden.

40
00:02:01,171 --> 00:02:09,729
(Beau) They were called dragons, and they
brought with them fire and hatred.

41
00:02:09,730 --> 00:02:12,850
(Beau) But humankind fought back.

42
00:02:12,851 --> 00:02:19,849
(Beau) They created battle machines
and Those machines created more

43
00:02:19,850 --> 00:02:25,650
(Beau) machines, and when those
machines failed, they made pacts with

44
00:02:25,651 --> 00:02:34,370
(Beau) demons in the darkest places of the
world and birthed unspeakable monsters.

45
00:02:34,371 --> 00:02:38,130
(Beau) With their champions
astride them, the humans

46
00:02:38,131 --> 00:02:43,090
(Beau) turned the tide of war and slew
the dragons by the thousands.

47
00:02:43,091 --> 00:02:45,690
(Beau) From their husks, the humans created.

48
00:02:45,770 --> 00:02:50,296
(Beau) Engines whose parts
never rusted or broke,

49
00:02:50,297 --> 00:02:54,570
(Beau) whose pistons operated
ceaselessly, and whose

50
00:02:54,571 --> 00:02:59,290
(Beau) combustion was interminable,
irradiating our world with.

51
00:03:01,630 --> 00:03:05,210
(Beau) that allowed them to wield terrible magics.

52
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:13,120
(Beau) The war raged for a century more.

53
00:03:13,121 --> 00:03:17,040
(Beau) As humankind and dragonkind
ground their numbers

54
00:03:17,041 --> 00:03:20,640
(Beau) to dust, the dragons
summoned the last of their

55
00:03:20,641 --> 00:03:25,200
(Beau) spite and scorched the
lands with it and vanished.

56
00:03:25,201 --> 00:03:29,280
(Beau) Their only remains, the
dragon engines used to

57
00:03:29,281 --> 00:03:32,930
(Beau) power the last bastions
of hope in a dying world.

58
00:03:49,810 --> 00:03:55,930
(Scott) If you could see past the scars, if you
could look beyond the tumors and craters.

59
00:03:58,555 --> 00:04:03,170
(Scott) If you could peer through the stinging
grit and torn soul of Nash Maggard.

60
00:04:04,880 --> 00:04:10,940
(Scott) You'd find light, blinding,
rending, destructive, terrible light.

61
00:04:15,095 --> 00:04:17,070
(Scott) Look deeper, and you
would find a man who could

62
00:04:17,071 --> 00:04:22,910
(Scott) blot out the very sun and take this
land beyond the repair of man or machine.

63
00:04:25,760 --> 00:04:28,830
(Scott) One who could bring pure and
permanent darkness with his curse.

64
00:04:30,560 --> 00:04:33,410
(Scott) taking this decaying,
festering world to its final rest.

65
00:04:37,530 --> 00:04:42,400
(Scott) But if you look yet deeper at Nash
Maggard, there is more than this.

66
00:04:44,230 --> 00:04:47,570
(Scott) you would find a spark
of something like salvation.

67
00:04:48,725 --> 00:04:51,970
(Scott) Something like redemption.

68
00:04:51,971 --> 00:04:53,950
(Scott) Something small, but able.

69
00:04:55,185 --> 00:04:58,970
(Scott) Perhaps willing to face down the
darker temptations that surround it.

70
00:05:02,065 --> 00:05:05,790
(Scott) Indeed, there may yet
be a time when the name

71
00:05:05,791 --> 00:05:08,670
(Scott) Maggard is spoken in
this desolation without

72
00:05:08,671 --> 00:05:12,540
(Scott) revulsion and the flow of
tears from frightened children.

73
00:05:14,425 --> 00:05:16,950
(Scott) Perhaps there will come
a time when he will be

74
00:05:16,951 --> 00:05:19,970
(Scott) remembered as something
more, something better.

75
00:05:22,720 --> 00:05:24,720
(Scott) That day is not now.

76
00:05:24,721 --> 00:05:25,760
(Scott) His path is new.

77
00:05:27,360 --> 00:05:30,140
(Scott) And his countless years in the
solar mines are well behind him.

78
00:05:32,190 --> 00:05:36,220
(Scott) In his leaving wake there lies devastation
of the wicked and the righteous.

79
00:05:38,390 --> 00:05:41,590
(Scott) His escape left none to
tell what they had seen.

80
00:05:41,591 --> 00:05:45,430
(Scott) History would never know what
happened there, but Nash knew.

81
00:05:45,530 --> 00:05:46,610
(Scott) And that would haunt him.

82
00:05:48,270 --> 00:05:51,390
(Scott) But it would also fuel
him, like the ancient oil

83
00:05:51,391 --> 00:05:55,040
(Scott) grounds did for the upright
men before the fall a millennia ago.

84
00:05:58,370 --> 00:06:00,610
(Scott) It is near dawn now.

85
00:06:00,611 --> 00:06:02,930
(Scott) He stamps out the
remains of his cook fire with

86
00:06:02,931 --> 00:06:05,690
(Scott) his tattered boot and looks
to the west with one eye.

87
00:06:07,630 --> 00:06:11,310
(Scott) The other burns, sightless
and dormant, and waits

88
00:06:11,311 --> 00:06:14,080
(Scott) for the next chance to
play its dark and terrible role.

89
00:06:16,480 --> 00:06:18,480
(Scott) He takes his staff from
its resting place among

90
00:06:18,481 --> 00:06:21,120
(Scott) the stones, throws his
threadbare satchel over

91
00:06:21,121 --> 00:06:24,730
(Scott) his pure shoulder, and puts
the rising sun to his back.

92
00:06:27,730 --> 00:06:31,890
(Scott) He knows not who he will meet, nor
what he will face, and he doesn't care.

93
00:06:31,891 --> 00:06:37,210
(Scott) What comes will come, and when
it does, Nash will be ready to face it.

94
00:06:40,080 --> 00:06:42,000
(Scott) He takes a final look
over his shoulder, back

95
00:06:42,001 --> 00:06:44,990
(Scott) toward the Blood Canyons,
the only home he'd ever known.

96
00:06:46,580 --> 00:06:47,780
(Scott) He can never go back.

97
00:06:47,781 --> 00:06:49,540
(Scott) He knows this.

98
00:06:49,541 --> 00:06:52,190
(Scott) And yet his heart still
aches for the one long lost.

99
00:06:53,175 --> 00:06:57,700
(Scott) Perhaps a story for a different time.

100
00:06:57,701 --> 00:07:00,815
(Scott) His boots left dusty
footprints as he walked,

101
00:07:00,816 --> 00:07:03,330
(Scott) the only evidence that
Nash Maggard was here.

102
00:07:04,910 --> 00:07:07,150
(Scott) They would soon be blown
to oblivion by the next.

103
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:09,230
(Scott) storm.

104
00:07:09,231 --> 00:07:12,670
(Scott) Like a chapter in the old
books, his page was turning.

105
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:16,560
(Scott) And he was turning with it.

106
00:07:16,561 --> 00:07:19,100
(Scott) And for now, that was enough.

107
00:07:27,900 --> 00:07:30,210
(Kristen) The light fades.

108
00:07:30,211 --> 00:07:31,290
(Kristen) The vision dims.

109
00:07:32,515 --> 00:07:36,750
(Kristen) All that remains are memories.

110
00:07:36,751 --> 00:07:42,910
(Kristen) We tell of a time of chaos,
ruined dreams, this wasted land.

111
00:07:42,911 --> 00:07:49,070
(Kristen) But there are those of us that speak
of hope, the way the world could be.

112
00:07:49,071 --> 00:07:53,310
(Kristen) To recall what it was like, we
have to go back to the other time.

113
00:07:53,311 --> 00:07:56,030
(Kristen) When this world was blue and green, and the

114
00:07:56,230 --> 00:07:57,250
(Kristen) desert sprouted life.

115
00:07:58,485 --> 00:08:00,850
(Kristen) Gone now.

116
00:08:01,050 --> 00:08:02,080
(Kristen) Swept away.

117
00:08:04,070 --> 00:08:06,710
(Kristen) For reasons long forgotten,
mighty dragons came

118
00:08:06,711 --> 00:08:10,950
(Kristen) from beyond and touched
off a Blaze which engulfed it all.

119
00:08:10,951 --> 00:08:14,550
(Kristen) Without a means to fight,
the humans were nothing.

120
00:08:14,551 --> 00:08:17,510
(Kristen) They were made of naught but straw.

121
00:08:17,511 --> 00:08:20,630
(Kristen) The thundering creatures
roared and pillaged.

122
00:08:20,631 --> 00:08:24,310
(Kristen) Heroes fought and fought and fought.

123
00:08:24,311 --> 00:08:27,750
(Kristen) But nothing could stem the conflagration.

124
00:08:27,751 --> 00:08:30,150
(Kristen) The world crumbled.

125
00:08:30,151 --> 00:08:31,510
(Kristen) Life exploded.

126
00:08:31,511 --> 00:08:32,990
(Kristen) A whirlwind of death.

127
00:08:33,829 --> 00:08:35,870
(Kristen) A firestorm of fear.

128
00:08:35,871 --> 00:08:39,150
(Kristen) Men began to feed on men.

129
00:08:39,151 --> 00:08:40,659
(Kristen) For those that survived,

130
00:08:41,635 --> 00:08:44,880
(Kristen) It was a nightmare with no end.

131
00:08:47,029 --> 00:08:49,710
(Kristen) Only those brave enough
to seek help, desperate

132
00:08:49,711 --> 00:08:54,640
(Kristen) enough to live, would find the
demons and make the dark pit.

133
00:08:56,105 --> 00:08:59,330
(Kristen) The demons took over
the land ready to wage war

134
00:08:59,331 --> 00:09:02,050
(Kristen) and win back the world
from the dragons, and in

135
00:09:02,051 --> 00:09:06,610
(Kristen) this maelstrom of decay
the tieflings emerged

136
00:09:06,611 --> 00:09:12,530
(Kristen) powerful and strong men and women, the
warriors designed to destroy the dragons.

137
00:09:12,531 --> 00:09:13,820
(Kristen) In the roar of battle,

138
00:09:16,060 --> 00:09:20,720
(Kristen) We lost everything and
became a shell of what we were.

139
00:09:22,270 --> 00:09:24,830
(Kristen) A burnt out, desolate race.

140
00:09:24,831 --> 00:09:28,190
(Kristen) A race haunted by the demons of the past.

141
00:09:28,191 --> 00:09:30,750
(Kristen) A race that wandered
out into the waste land.

142
00:09:32,960 --> 00:09:38,400
(Kristen) And it was here, in this blighted
place, that we learned to live again.

143
00:09:38,401 --> 00:09:43,450
(Kristen) And so began our journey to
right the wrong, to erase the past.

144
00:09:44,825 --> 00:09:47,400
(Kristen) Among us, we found a new promise.

145
00:09:47,401 --> 00:09:51,560
(Kristen) The tiefling who would travel
back and complete the pact.

146
00:09:51,561 --> 00:09:52,680
(Kristen) Hope.

147
00:09:52,681 --> 00:09:55,480
(Kristen) And just as my ancestral
stories have foretold,

148
00:09:55,481 --> 00:09:59,960
(Kristen) I've traveled far beyond the
reach of society's misconceptions.

149
00:09:59,961 --> 00:10:03,160
(Kristen) The dragon engines,
the precious engines, are

150
00:10:03,161 --> 00:10:06,200
(Kristen) hidden across the world,
and I'm going to find

151
00:10:06,201 --> 00:10:11,560
(Kristen) one, head back to the past, and
restore this world to its former glory.

152
00:10:11,561 --> 00:10:13,010
(Kristen) The current wasteland!

153
00:10:14,770 --> 00:10:17,570
(Kristen) This is the last we'll ever see of it.

154
00:10:17,571 --> 00:10:20,610
(Kristen) It will live on only in our memories.

155
00:10:25,220 --> 00:10:30,500
(John) My name is Stanley Billings, and
I'm going to save this wasteland.

156
00:10:30,501 --> 00:10:33,140
(John) Take a look around it,
and you'll see what I've

157
00:10:33,141 --> 00:10:37,840
(John) seen my entire life
brutality, hopelessness, death.

158
00:10:39,170 --> 00:10:41,330
(John) I was once right there with you.

159
00:10:41,331 --> 00:10:46,140
(John) I've had my fair share of bad choices
just to see another miserable day.

160
00:10:47,790 --> 00:10:50,990
(John) That all changed when I found the artifact.

161
00:10:50,991 --> 00:10:53,950
(John) An ancient Tome of forgotten knowledge that

162
00:10:53,951 --> 00:10:59,230
(John) opened my eyes to not only
what was, but also what could be.

163
00:10:59,231 --> 00:11:02,830
(John) I learned the words that
we had long forgotten,

164
00:11:02,831 --> 00:11:10,430
(John) words like society, Liberty, and
the path to these ideals government.

165
00:11:10,431 --> 00:11:17,290
(John) You see, it's the lawless nature of this
world that has held it in chaos for so long.

166
00:11:18,010 --> 00:11:21,130
(John) All it needs is the right
person, willing to do

167
00:11:21,131 --> 00:11:25,770
(John) whatever it takes to push
that chaos back into order.

168
00:11:25,771 --> 00:11:27,930
(John) Am I the man to do this?

169
00:11:27,931 --> 00:11:30,490
(John) You bet your ass I am.

170
00:11:30,491 --> 00:11:35,740
(John) After all, I'm Stanley Billings,
and I'm gonna save this wasteland.

171
00:11:41,430 --> 00:11:45,270
(Kyle) Between the rocky crags
of Vaerthicha and the

172
00:11:45,271 --> 00:11:49,590
(Kyle) endless wastes of Ka
Egro, there lives a creature

173
00:11:49,591 --> 00:11:54,870
(Kyle) of untold strength and
tremendous fortitude.

174
00:11:54,871 --> 00:12:03,100
(Kyle) A raw, untamed pillar of rocky scales
and muscle, blasted by sand and sun.

175
00:12:04,910 --> 00:12:08,270
(Kyle) Born to the barbarous
lizard folk, whose deeds go

176
00:12:08,271 --> 00:12:13,790
(Kyle) unseen by civilized eyes,
Borel Rasvim Kurek, the

177
00:12:13,791 --> 00:12:18,910
(Kyle) bountiful slaughter, remains
the last of his desert kin.

178
00:12:20,530 --> 00:12:25,650
(Kyle) Seven feet tall, his gait a brawny swagger,

179
00:12:25,651 --> 00:12:30,450
(Kyle) Vorrell now ventures towards
the dilapidated town of Dusthill.

180
00:12:30,451 --> 00:12:35,970
(Kyle) A massive bloody haunch of
meat slung atop his broad shoulder.

181
00:12:35,971 --> 00:12:41,730
(Kyle) An adequate trade for the life giving
waters that sustain his desert wanderings.

182
00:12:41,731 --> 00:12:46,450
(Kyle) But fate seeks to break his isolation.

183
00:12:46,451 --> 00:12:49,650
(Kyle) The desert stars tell of great change.

184
00:12:49,730 --> 00:12:55,330
(Kyle) Ancient machines and beasts
rise from their dormant slumber.

185
00:12:55,331 --> 00:13:00,130
(Kyle) The world was once shaped by steel and oil.

186
00:13:00,131 --> 00:13:04,380
(Kyle) It will now be forged with bone and sinew.

187
00:13:06,629 --> 00:13:11,360
(Kyle) Behold, the great adventure
of our time begins now.

